    <help><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Combines two or more booleans into one, for example to run a workflow step
only when several conditions hold. Connect the result to the ``when`` input of
a step, or to any boolean parameter. Add more inputs with "Insert Boolean".

**Operators**

========== ================================================================
Operator   Result is true when
========== ================================================================
AND        all inputs are true
OR         at least one input is true
NAND       at least one input is false (the opposite of AND)
NOR        no input is true (the opposite of OR)
XOR        an odd number of inputs are true
Exactly 1  exactly one input is true
All equal  all inputs are true, or all inputs are false
========== ================================================================

XOR and "Exactly one" agree for two inputs but differ for more: with three
true inputs XOR is true (three is odd) and "Exactly one" is false.

**Truth table for two inputs**

===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ========= =========
A     B     AND   OR    NAND  NOR   XOR   Exactly 1 All equal
===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ========= =========
true  true  true  true  false false false false     true
true  false false true  true  false true  true      false
false true  false true  true  false true  true      false
false false false false true  true  false false     true
===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ===== ========= =========

@NULL_HANDLING_HELP@

Treating unset inputs as true makes AND ignore them; treating them as false
makes OR ignore them. If every input is unset, all of them get the substituted
value.

To negate a single boolean, use **Invert boolean parameter**.
    ]]></help>
